<title>BELGIUM: EU clears Ferrostaal buy of DSD Dillinger.</title>
<headline>EU clears Ferrostaal buy of DSD Dillinger.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it had cleared the acquisition by Ferrostaal AG, a subsidiary of German machinery group MAN, of the full control of DSD Dillinger Stahlbau GmbH.</p>
<p>Ferrostaal currently owns 38.1 percent of the shares in DSD.</p>
<p>It is buying the remaining shares from its subsidiary SGI Saarlaendische, the Commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>The operation is part of the restructuring of MAN's industrial units.</p>
<p>The Commission said the activities of Ferrostaal and DSD overlaped only in the field of construction of low pressure containers where the combined market share will be about 10 percent in Germany and five percent in the European Union.</p>
<p>But this was of no serious concern given the presence of strong competitors.</p>
</text>
